      "id": "fpq_102",
      "kind": "fpq",
      "input_question": "I've recently noticed a dark spot under my toenail. I'm not too worried since I always wear shoes and it's not exposed to the sun. Could it just be a bruise that's taking a long time to heal?",
      "target_excerpt": "The premise that \"it's not exposed to the sun\" might be considered a false premise in this context because dark spots under toenails can sometimes be caused by melanoma, which is a type of skin cancer. While exposure to sunlight is a known risk factor for many types of skin cancer, melanoma can develop in areas that are not directly exposed to the sun, such as under toenails.",
